```ts
window.addEventListener('message', (event) => {
  const msg = event.data;

  if (msg.type === 'galyleo:requestSave') {
    // Respond by asking the editor for the current contents
    this._postMessage({ type: 'getContents' });
  }

  if (msg.type === 'contents') {
    this._model.fromJSON(msg.contents);
    this._model.dirty = false;
  }

  if (msg.type === 'contentChanged') {
    this._model.dirty = true;
  }
});
```

---

And that’s it — your editor initiates the save at the right moment, and the extension responds smoothly.

